From: syhhyl
Subject: [PATCH] fix(decode): clear gpWen for rd == x0 in PseudoDecodeChannel

`csrr x0, vl` / `csrr x0, vlenb` are legal pure reads: the value is read and
discarded because x0 is hardwired to zero.  The vl/vlenb pseudo decode channel
takes gpWen straight from the uop table, so rename sees rfWen = 1 with
ldest = x0, allocates a physical register for x0, and writes the speculative
RAT entry of x0.  With assertions enabled this trips
"rfWen cannot be 1 when Int regfile ldest is 0" and "pdest for $0 should be 0".

Gate gpWen with rd != 0, exactly like SimpleDecodeChannel, VsetDecoder and
VectorDecodeChannel already do.

Upstream equivalent: 429980ea228c ("fix(decode): add support of out-of-order
CSRR instructions execution", PR #6779), which applies this line together with
the CSRR OoO rework.

---
 src/main/scala/xiangshan/backend/vector/Decoder/DecodeChannel/PseudoDecodeChannel.scala | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main/scala/xiangshan/backend/vector/Decoder/DecodeChannel/PseudoDecodeChannel.scala b/src/main/scala/xiangshan/backend/vector/Decoder/DecodeChannel/PseudoDecodeChannel.scala
--- a/src/main/scala/xiangshan/backend/vector/Decoder/DecodeChannel/PseudoDecodeChannel.scala
+++ b/src/main/scala/xiangshan/backend/vector/Decoder/DecodeChannel/PseudoDecodeChannel.scala
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ class PseudoDecodeChannel(
   out.bits.lsrc1 := instBitFields.RS1
   out.bits.lsrc2 := instBitFields.RS2
   out.bits.ldest := instBitFields.RD
-  out.bits.gpWen := bundle(gpWenField)
+  out.bits.gpWen := bundle(gpWenField) && instBitFields.RD =/= 0.U
   out.bits.fpWen := bundle(fpWenField)
   out.bits.noSpec := bundle(noSpecField)
   out.bits.blockBack := bundle(blockBackField)
